planted in the 1920s and is native to Spain and Italy. Pinus pinea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALone_Pine_cemetery_May_2002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lone_Pine_Wattle_Park.jpg/500px-Lone_Pine_Wattle_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lone_Pine_Wattle_Park.jpg/500px-Lone_Pine_Wattle_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Lone Pine planted at Wattle Park (Melbourne) in 1933 is one of the originals grown from seed from the cone collected by Thomas Keith McDowell. It comes from the solitary \"Lone Pine\". Pinus brutia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALone_Pine_Wattle_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lone_Pine_at_the_AWM.jpg/500px-Lone_Pine_at_the_AWM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lone_Pine_at_the_AWM.jpg/500px-Lone_Pine_at_the_AWM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lone Pine at the Australian War Memorial (Canberra) is an Aleppo pine Pinus halepensis. It was planted in 1934 by the Duke of Gloucester. The seed came from a cone collected by  Benjamin Smith from a Turkish trench. Aleppo pine is not native to the Gallipoli peninsula but was brought in by the Turks to reinforce their fortifications.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALone_Pine_at_the_AWM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Lone_Pine_tree_at_entrance_to_Oatley_Park.JPG/120px-Lone_Pine_tree_at_entrance_to_Oatley_Park.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Lone_Pine_tree_at_entrance_to_Oatley_Park.JPG/250px-Lone_Pine_tree_at_entr